<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Line and bar charts for 2023 and 2024 show monthly rainfall and air temperatures. Rainfall is in striped bars and temperature is a red line. The shaded area represents the temperature range. Rainfall varies monthly, while temperature generally rises from February to July, then stabilizes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (\(A\) Two histograms with fitted normal distribution curves. The left shows D-values at 10°C with mean 0.279 and right at 15°C with mean 0.378. Both include standard deviation, kurtosis, and skewness. \(B\) Two scatter plots with regression lines. The left plot for 10°C shows \\\( R^2 = 0.9337 \\\), and the right for 15°C shows \\\( R^2 = 0.9811 \\\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Dendrogram showcasing hierarchical clustering, alongside a heatmap with color gradients from blue to red, indicating values from 0.12 to 0.66. Sections are labeled I to IV, categorizing clustered data.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Bar charts comparing emergence percentages of different treatments under two conditions: extreme cold by early sowing \(A\), and mild low temperature early sowing \(B\). Each treatment is represented by numbered bars with varying colors. Bars are annotated with letters indicating statistical differences. Condition A generally shows lower emergence percentages compared to condition B.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (A heatmap displays a matrix with columns labeled EP-1, EP-2, GWPS-1, GWPS-2, and D-value. Cells range from red to blue, indicating values between zero and one. A color scale on the right shows red for high values \(0.93\) and blue for low values \(-0.07\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Heat map with a dendrogram on the right, displaying hierarchical clustering of data. The left column shows varying color intensities from red to blue, corresponding to numerical values. Cluster groups are labeled with Roman numerals I to IV. A color scale indicates values from 0.09 to 0.86, with red representing higher values and blue representing lower values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot showing the evaluation of D-value in germination tests under controlled conditions versus field trials. Data points are scattered around a line with the equation y = 0.9559x + 0.1535, indicating a positive correlation. The correlation coefficient is R = 0.687.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Two scatter plots compare D-value evaluations. Plot A shows D-values in germination tests versus physiological indicators, with a line of best fit y=0.593x + 0.1633 and R=0.872. Plot B shows D-values in field trials versus physiological indicators, with a line of best fit y=0.883x + 0.1596 and R=0.841. Both show positive correlations using blue data points.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot showing the relationship between predicted values based on physiological indicators and evaluation of D-values in field trials. Points fit closely along the line with equation y = 1.0022x - 0.0009. The correlation coefficient is R = 0.976.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
